@startuml SH04_Coding_Practice
title SyntacHire AI - Coding Problem Execution and Submission
autonumber
actor Candidate
participant "React Client" as Client
participant "Express API" as API
participant "Problem Controller" as Problems
participant "Judge0 RapidAPI" as RapidAPI
participant "Public Judge0 CE" as PublicJudge0
database MongoDB as DB

Candidate -> Client: Open a coding problem
Client -> API: GET /api/problems/:id
API -> Problems: Load problem and candidate solved state
Problems -> DB: Read Problem and UserDSAProgress
DB --> Problems: Problem and saved status
Problems --> API: Problem details
API --> Client: Problem data
Client --> Candidate: Show problem, editor, and examples

== Run code with custom or sample input ==
Candidate -> Client: Click Run
Client -> RapidAPI: POST /submissions?wait=true (source, language, input)
alt RapidAPI execution succeeds
  RapidAPI --> Client: stdout, stderr, status, runtime
else RapidAPI fails or unavailable
  Client -> PublicJudge0: POST /submissions?wait=true (source, language, input)
  PublicJudge0 --> Client: stdout, stderr, status, runtime
end
Client --> Candidate: Display execution result

== Submit against all example test cases ==
Candidate -> Client: Click Submit
loop For each example test case
  Client -> RapidAPI: Execute wrapped solution with test input
  alt RapidAPI execution succeeds
    RapidAPI --> Client: Test output and status
  else RapidAPI fails or unavailable
    Client -> PublicJudge0: Execute wrapped solution with test input
    PublicJudge0 --> Client: Test output and status
  end
  Client -> Client: Compare output with expected result
end
alt All test cases pass
  Client -> API: PATCH /api/problems/:id { status: solved }
  API -> Problems: Save solved status for authenticated user
  Problems -> DB: Upsert UserDSAProgress.solvedProblems
  DB --> Problems: Progress saved
  Problems --> API: Updated problem status
  API --> Client: Solved status
  Client --> Candidate: Show Accepted and update progress
else One or more test cases fail
  Client --> Candidate: Show wrong answer or runtime/compile error
end

opt Candidate toggles a problem bookmark
  Candidate -> Client: Toggle bookmark
  Client -> API: PATCH /api/problems/:id/bookmark
  API -> Problems: Toggle problem bookmark
  Problems -> DB: Save Problem.isBookmarked
  DB --> Problems: Updated problem
  Problems --> API: Bookmark state
  API --> Client: Updated bookmark
  Client --> Candidate: Display bookmark state
end
@enduml

@startuml SH05_Resume_Analysis
title SyntacHire AI - Resume Analysis and History
autonumber
actor Candidate
participant "React Client" as Client
participant "Express API" as API
participant "Auth Middleware" as Auth
participant "Resume Controller" as Resume
participant "PDF Parser" as PDF
participant "Google Gemini AI" as Gemini
database MongoDB as DB

Candidate -> Client: Upload PDF and choose target role
Client -> API: POST /api/resume/analyze (multipart PDF, Bearer token)
API -> Auth: Verify JWT
Auth --> API: Authenticated user ID
API -> Resume: Validate PDF and analyze request
Resume -> PDF: Extract text from PDF
PDF --> Resume: Resume text
alt PDF valid and text extracted
  Resume -> Gemini: Analyze resume against target role
  Gemini --> Resume: ATS score, skills, gaps, suggestions, summary
  Resume -> DB: Save resume text and analysis
  DB --> Resume: Saved analysis record
  Resume --> API: Analysis result
  API --> Client: Resume analysis
  Client --> Candidate: Display ATS score and recommendations
else Invalid PDF or no readable text
  Resume --> API: PDF validation error
  API --> Client: Upload/parse error
  Client --> Candidate: Show error
end

== Browse resume history ==
Candidate -> Client: Open resume history
Client -> API: GET /api/resume/history + Bearer token
API -> Auth: Verify JWT
Auth --> API: Authenticated user ID
API -> DB: Find resume analyses for user, newest first
DB --> API: Resume analysis records
API --> Client: Resume history
Client --> Candidate: Display analysis history

opt Candidate deletes an analysis record
  Candidate -> Client: Delete selected record
  Client -> API: DELETE /api/resume/:id + Bearer token
  API -> Auth: Verify JWT
  Auth --> API: Authenticated user ID
  API -> DB: Delete record belonging to this user
  DB --> API: Deletion result
  API --> Client: Success or not found
  Client --> Candidate: Refresh history
end
@enduml

@startuml SH06_Mock_Interview
title SyntacHire AI - Adaptive Mock Interview Session
autonumber
actor Candidate
participant "React Client" as Client
participant "Express API" as API
participant "Interview Controller" as Interview
participant "Question Generator" as QuestionGen
participant "Gemini Evaluation Service" as Evaluation
participant "Google Gemini AI" as Gemini
participant "Audio Upload Storage" as Audio
database MongoDB as DB

Candidate -> Client: Configure role, interview type, and response mode
Client -> API: POST /api/interview/start
API -> Interview: Start session (optional JWT)
Interview -> DB: Load resume skills and interview history
DB --> Interview: Candidate context and prior performance
Interview -> QuestionGen: Generate first question for role and difficulty
QuestionGen -> Gemini: Request personalized interview question
Gemini --> QuestionGen: First question
QuestionGen --> Interview: Question data
Interview -> DB: Create in-progress Interview record
DB --> Interview: Interview ID and saved session
Interview --> API: Interview ID and first question
API --> Client: Session started
Client --> Candidate: Display first question

loop For each submitted interview answer
  Candidate -> Client: Submit text answer and/or audio recording
  Client -> API: POST /api/interview/:id/submit (multipart form)
  opt Audio recording supplied
    API -> Audio: Save recording file
    Audio --> API: Recording URL
  end
  API -> Interview: Validate session and question index
  Interview -> Gemini: Evaluate answer for role and question
  Gemini --> Interview: Scores, strengths, gaps, and feedback
  Interview -> Interview: Adapt difficulty; decide whether to probe
  opt Another question or follow-up is required
    Interview -> DB: Load candidate context and session questions
    DB --> Interview: Prior questions and performance
    Interview -> QuestionGen: Generate next or follow-up question
    QuestionGen -> Gemini: Request adaptive question
    Gemini --> QuestionGen: Next question
    QuestionGen --> Interview: Question data
  end
  Interview -> DB: Save answer, audio URL, evaluation, and next question
  DB --> Interview: Updated session
  Interview --> API: Evaluation, feedback, and optional next question
  API --> Client: Feedback and adaptive difficulty
  Client --> Candidate: Display scorecard and next question
end

Candidate -> Client: Finish interview
Client -> API: PATCH /api/interview/:id/finish
API -> Interview: Aggregate session scores and topics
Interview -> Gemini: Generate final performance report
Gemini --> Interview: Summary, feedback, and recommended topics
Interview -> DB: Mark completed and save final report
DB --> Interview: Completed interview
Interview --> API: Final report
API --> Client: Interview result
Client --> Candidate: Display completed scorecard

== Review interview history ==
Candidate -> Client: Open interview history
Client -> API: GET /api/interview/history
API -> Interview: Fetch interview sessions (optional JWT)
Interview -> DB: Query sessions for authenticated user
DB --> Interview: Interview history
Interview --> API: History records
API --> Client: Interview history
Client --> Candidate: Display past sessions and reports
@enduml

